# Line endings.
#
# The repository stores Python, docs and data as LF. One file -
# coordinates/inspector.py - was committed with CRLF under a core.autocrlf
# setting that preserved it, which made every subsequent edit to the most
# important coordinate-science module in the tree look like a full-file
# rewrite and made git blame useless on it.
#
# Declaring the convention here fixes it for good: checkout writes LF
# whatever a contributor's core.autocrlf says, so the same edit produces the
# same diff on every machine.
*.py text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.csv text eol=lf

# Windows batch files are executed by cmd.exe and are conventionally CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf
